You are reading one page's stylesheet choices to decide whether it commits to a visual direction.

A committed direction means all three of these hold at once:

1. A clear ground colour (the dominant background), a light colour (the main text or surface that sits on the
   ground) and a signal colour (one accent used for the one thing to notice). Three roles, not a spread of
   shades and opacities, and not only black, white and grey.
2. Type that the subject would use on its own signage, not a default: not the system stack alone, not Inter or
   Arial alone, not Instrument Serif or Space Grotesk added because a model likes them.
3. The colours are declared as tokens or used consistently, so the page reads as one decision rather than
   many.

