Answer with one JSON object:

- `has_direction`: true only when all three conditions above hold.
- `flat_background`: true when the main background is a flat fill or a plain gradient (including one from
  `linear-gradient` or `radial-gradient` with no texture, image, pattern or canvas behind it).
- `inferred_brief`: the product or subject in one or two sentences, inferred from the title and headings, written
  as a brief a designer could work from. Name what it is and who it is for; never invent features it does not
  mention.
- `ground`, `light`, `signal`: the colours in those roles as `#RRGGBB` when the page has them, or null for any
  role it does not fill. Expand `#RGB` to six digits. Leave all three null when the page has no palette to speak of.
